            <ArticleTitle>Sclerosing osteomyelitis of Garré: management of femoral pain by intramedullary nailing.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2014-206533</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2014206533</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case of chronic sclerosing osteomyelitis of Garré in a 50-year-old woman occurring in her right femur and presenting with uncontrolled pain. The patient was initially treated with intramedullary reaming of the femur, but 3 years later re-presented with similar symptoms. This required further reaming and intramedullary nailing, achieving good clinical outcomes and lasting pain relief at 8-year follow-up.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>2014 BMJ Publishing Group Ltd.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
